From: Lukasz Smurawski <lukasz.smurawski@grinn-global.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ina423x: use each channel's shunt gain

The CONFIG2 setup loop always checks channel 0, causing all ADC range bits
to follow the first channel's gain. Use the loop index so every channel is
configured from its own shunt-gain value.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Lukasz Smurawski <lukasz.smurawski@grinn-global.com>
---
 ina423x.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ina423x.c b/ina423x.c
index fa7db48..922d127 100644
--- a/ina423x.c
+++ b/ina423x.c
@@ -1128,7 +1128,7 @@ static int ina423x_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	config2 = data->config->config2_default;
 
 	for(i = 0; i < INA423x_NUM_CHANNELS; i++) {
-		if (data->gain[0] == 1) {
+		if (data->gain[i] == 1) {
 			config2 |= INA423x_CONFIG2_RANGE(i+1); /* ADCRANGE = 1 is /1 */
 		}
 	}
-- 
